  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>This test is useful for detection of antibodies to Schistosoma species.<br>Negative: the absence of antibodies to Schistosoma suggests that the patient has not been exposed to the trematode. A<br>single negative result should not be used to rule-out infection with Schistosoma species.<br>Positive - Absorbance reading greater or equal to 0.2 OD units.<br>&nbsp;Negative - Absorbance reading less than 0.2 OD units.<br>Equivocal: consider repeat testing on a new serum sample in 1 to 2 weeks.<br>Positive: results suggest infection with Schistosoma. False-positive results may occur in setting of infection with other<br>helminthes, including with Echinococcus or Taenia species results should be considered alongside other clinical findings and<br>exposure history.<br>Limitation:<br>1. Sensitivity for detection of antibodies to each of Schistosoma species cannot be evaluated for this assay.<br>2. Some patients may remain seropositive by this assay following treatment an clearance of infection.<br>3. Positive results should be confirmed with other laboratory finding [e.g. ova and parent examination) clinical symptom<br>and sutable exposure history.</p>",
